cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OphthoImageTools: ImageJ & MATLAB tools for ophthalmic imaging analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file and the companion editorial."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pichi"
    given-names: "Francesco"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7357-4166"
    affiliation: "University of Toronto, Department of Ophthalmology and Vision Science; Kensington Eye Institute, Toronto, Canada"
  - family-names: "Carreño"
    given-names: "Ester"
    affiliation: "Department of Ophthalmology, Hospital Universitario La Paz, Madrid, Spain"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OphthoImageTools/OphthoImageTools"
url: "https://github.com/OphthoImageTools/OphthoImageTools"
abstract: >
  OphthoImageTools is an open collection of ImageJ/Fiji macros and MATLAB
  scripts for objective, reproducible analysis of ophthalmic images, with a
  focus on uveitis biomarkers: keratic precipitate volumetry on AS-OCT,
  ultra-widefield fundus depigmentation in Vogt–Koyanagi–Harada disease,
  macrophage-like cell density on en face OCT angiography, and automatic
  ETDRS-grid sectoral counting.
keywords:
  - uveitis
  - ophthalmology
  - image-analysis
